id: pm-wanwyc
title: Agent-task transcripts accept declared no-effect and partial-effect successful exits
description: "Greptile review on PR #1133 found that the new public transcript parser accepts only exit 0 for non-refusal steps even though pm's canonical command-exit SDK contract treats exit 6 no_effect and exit 7 partial_effect as successful for close-many and update-many. Reuse the canonical exit vocabulary, require the exit to be both successful and declared for the command, and add adversarial parser coverage."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[5]: agent-ux,"area:sdk",contracts,exit-codes,review-feedback
created_at: "2026-08-27T17:57:51.200Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-28T03:57:23.330Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-28T03:57:22.767Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-28T03:57:22.767Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: "Transcript steps accept exits 0, 6, and 7 only when the canonical command contract declares that successful exit; Refusal steps reject every successful exit; Non-bulk commands cannot claim successful effect-aware exits; Exact unit and full coverage gates pass"
parent: pm-8pnj
resolution: completed
expected_result: Transcripts accept every successful exit that the invoked command declares and reject undeclared or refusal-success contradictions.
actual_result: "Transcript validation now resolves the canonical command through the shared bootstrap scanner before consulting output and exit contracts, so boolean and value-consuming global prefixes preserve declared exits 6 and 7 while flag-only invocations fail closed."
