comments[6]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-27T17:57:51.200Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: all-status search for transcript successful exit, no_effect, and partial_effect found canonical exit-contract owner pm-hqa8g1 and the active transcript owner pm-8pnj, but no item for this PR #1133 parser contradiction; creating one review-caught child issue rather than duplicating either owner."
  "2026-08-27T18:17:28.812Z","harness:codex","Review resolution evidence for PR #1133: reused isPmSuccessfulExitCode plus the command-specific exit declaration; non-refusal transcripts accept exit 6/7 only for commands that declare them, refusals reject all successful exits, and the real corpus now executes close-many partial_effect=7 and no_effect=6 from stdout. Focused linked tests passed; full coverage passed 8,063 tests at exact 100/100/100/100; pnpm quality:static passed."
  "2026-08-27T22:34:58.312Z","harness:codex","Lifecycle reconciliation: the historical docs_add event is immutable and remains visible after its original close/release. Ownership is now explicitly reacquired before this corrective evidence entry; future closeout metadata must precede close and release."
  "2026-08-28T03:22:47.799Z","harness:codex","Review wording correction: the changelog is generated from PM titles. Updated this canonical title to state the implemented behavior: non-refusal transcript steps accept no_effect and partial_effect only when the invoked command declares those successful exits. Refusal steps and undeclared effect exits remain rejected."
  "2026-08-28T03:44:19.934Z","harness:codex","TDD red evidence: node scripts/run-tests.mjs test -- tests/unit/sdk/output-contracts.spec.ts failed exactly at the bulk-effects transcript after adding --json before close-many and value-consuming --pm-path before update-many. The parser resolved args[0] as the command and rejected declared exit 6 before reaching the second case."
  "2026-08-28T03:57:21.590Z","harness:codex","Exact-head Greptile resolution evidence: the parser now reuses parseBootstrapCommandName instead of args[0], covers --json before close-many and --pm-path <value> before update-many, and rejects a flag-only invocation with no command. Focused output/transcript tests passed 28/28, bootstrap tests passed 99/99, the linked PM test passed, full coverage passed 585 files and 8,076 tests at statements 59,941/59,941, branches 45,130/45,130, functions 12,466/12,466, lines 57,722/57,722, and CI=1 pnpm quality:static passed."
learnings[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-27T18:17:29.321Z","harness:codex","A transport status is not synonymous with failure: parsing, stream selection, and transcript validation must share the canonical effect-aware exit contract so exits 6 and 7 remain successful without becoming globally legal for every command."
  "2026-08-28T03:57:22.139Z","harness:codex","Transcript contracts must derive command identity with the same bootstrap grammar as runtime dispatch; positional args[0] assumptions drift as soon as global flags are legal before a command."
